    "pidGuideTitle": "How to tune the PID",
    "@pidGuideTitle": {
        "description": "Title of the PID tuning guide"
    },
    "pidGuide": "1. Calibrate the sensors and check that all of them have contrast.\n2. Low speed (about 80-100), Ki = 0 and Kd = 0.\n3. Raise Kp until the robot follows the line but zigzags (the chart crosses the center from side to side). Then lower it a little.\n4. Raise Kd until the zigzag disappears. If the robot shakes or vibrates, Kd is too high.\n5. Raise the speed in steps of 10-20 and repeat 3 and 4. At higher speed it usually needs more Kd.\n6. Ki is rarely needed: use it, very small (0.0001), only if the robot always runs off-center on straights.\nCompare settings on the same piece of track: the lower the average error, the more centered the robot.",
    "@pidGuide": {
        "description": "Step by step PID tuning guide"
    }
